AP gross profit and non-GAAP gross profit margin are defined to exclude charges related to the stock-based compensation expense, and disaster (recovery) charges. See below for the reasons management excludes each item:\n\n• Stock-based compensation expense consists of equity awards granted based on the estimated fair value of those awards at grant date.", "remarks": ["We are being prudent with our spending and reduce operating expenses in the first half, as compared to the prior year period."]}

